<title>USA: US Plains wheat escapes further freeze damage-WSC.</title>
<headline>US Plains wheat escapes further freeze damage-WSC.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Overnight temperatures Monday in the U.S. Central Plains were not low enough to cause further damage to the hard red winter wheat crop, a U.S. meteorologist said.</p>
<p>&quot;Generally speaking in the Central Plains winter wheat Belt, there's no real problem out there this morning,&quot; said Joel Burgio, senior meteorolgist with Weather Services Corp in Lexington, Mass.</p>
<p>Low temperatures ranged from 30 to 42 degrees Fahrenheit with the low 40s seen some eastern areas of the Plains, Burgio said.</p>
